ISSUE #1389: register_models(model_aliases=) parameter

[CLOSED by simonw] labels: enhancement, plugins

I wanted to build a plugin that registers asynchronous versions of sync-only models. To do that I needed a way to intercept the list of registered models after they had been registered.

After some experiments the neatest way to do that turned out to be:

```python
@llm.hookimpl(trylast=True)
def register_models(register, model_aliases):
    for mwa in model_aliases:
        if mwa.model and not mwa.async_model:
            if isinstance(mwa.model, llm.KeyModel):
                mwa.async_model = AsyncKeyModelWrapper(mwa.model)
            else:
                mwa.async_model = AsyncModelWrapper(mwa.model)
```
So adding a `model_aliases` parameter to the existing `register_models()` hook that provides a list of all previously registered models, then using `trylast=True`.

